The java.lang.string.join() method concatenates the given elements with the delimiter and returns the concatenated string

class Gfg1 {
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        // delimiter is "<" and elements are "Four", "Five", "Six", "Seven"
        String gfg1 = String.join(" < ", "Four", "Five", "Six", "Seven");

        System.out.println(gfg1);
    }
}

Four < Five < Six < Seven
